usage: flair diffsplice [-h] --isoform_bed ISOFORM_BED --counts_matrix
                        COUNTS_MATRIX -o OUTPUT [-t THREADS] [--test]
                        [--min_samps_gene_expr MIN_SAMPS_GENE_EXPR]
                        [--min_samps_feature_expr MIN_SAMPS_FEATURE_EXPR]
                        [--min_gene_expr MIN_GENE_EXPR]
                        [--min_feature_expr MIN_FEATURE_EXPR] [--batch]
                        [--condition_a CONDITION_A]
                        [--condition_b CONDITION_B] [--overwrite_output]

Call alternative splicing events from isoforms and test them for differential
usage

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -t THREADS, --threads THREADS
                        number of threads for parallel DRIMSeq (default: 4)
  --test                run DRIMSeq statistical testing
  --min_samps_gene_expr MIN_SAMPS_GENE_EXPR
                        DRIMSeq dmFilter min_samps_gene_expr: minimum number
                        of samples that have coverage over an AS event
                        inclusion/exclusion; events with too few samples are
                        filtered out and not tested (default: 6)
  --min_samps_feature_expr MIN_SAMPS_FEATURE_EXPR
                        DRIMSeq dmFilter min_samps_feature_expr: minimum
                        number of samples expressing the inclusion of an AS
                        event; events with too few samples are filtered out
                        and not tested (default: 3)
  --min_gene_expr MIN_GENE_EXPR
                        DRIMSeq dmFilter min_gene_expr: minimum number of
                        reads covering an AS event inclusion/exclusion; events
                        with too few reads are filtered out and not tested
                        (default: 15)
  --min_feature_expr MIN_FEATURE_EXPR
                        DRIMSeq dmFilter min_feature_expr: minimum number of
                        reads covering an AS event inclusion; events with too
                        few reads are filtered out and not tested (default: 5)
  --batch               with --test, DRIMSeq will perform batch correction
  --condition_a CONDITION_A
                        implies --test. The reference condition, as named in
                        the counts matrix columns; the comparison is
                        --condition_b against this. With neither this nor
                        --condition_b given, the two conditions are taken in
                        sorted order
  --condition_b CONDITION_B
                        the condition compared against --condition_a
  --overwrite_output    overwrite files in an existing output directory

required named arguments:
  --isoform_bed ISOFORM_BED
                        isoforms in bed format
  --counts_matrix COUNTS_MATRIX
                        tab-delimited isoform count matrix from flair quantify
  -o OUTPUT, --output OUTPUT
                        output directory for tables and plots
